        "description": "<p>The hidden temple's maze contains chambers with artifacts and puzzles. Archaeologists need to recover the fifth most recently discovered artifact from chambers containing unsolved expert-level puzzles to prioritize excavation efforts. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: 'artifacts' and 'puzzles': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'artifacts' table includes the columns 'artifact_id', 'artifact_name', 'chamber_id', and 'discovery_date', representing unique artifact identifiers, artifact names, chamber identifiers, and discovery dates. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'puzzles' table includes the columns 'puzzle_id', 'chamber_id', 'puzzle_level', and 'solved_date', representing unique puzzle identifiers, chamber identifiers, puzzle difficulty levels, and solution dates (NULL if unsolved). &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identifies chambers with any 'Expert'‑level puzzles that remain unsolved.</li>\n<li>Retrieves artifacts located in those chambers.</li>\n<li>Orders them by 'discovery_date' descending and then 'artifact_id' ascending, and selects only the fifth artifact in that sequence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include the columns 'artifact_id', 'artifact_name', 'chamber_id', and 'discovery_date'.</p>",
