        "id": "569584",
        "title": "Mr. Perfect",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p class=\"\" data-start=\"23\" data-end=\"58\">Mr. Perfect, the beloved team leader at Bulldog Inc, is famous for his thoughtful leadership. He wants to optimize his team&rsquo;s workload by identifying \"sandwich dates\"&mdash;those tricky workdays squeezed between holidays when productivity dips. By spotting these dates early, he can plan lighter workloads or fun remote work days to keep morale high! he turns to you with a special request to find those dates. you are given a table 'holidays'.</p>\n<ul data-start=\"60\" data-end=\"206\">\n<li class=\"\" data-start=\"60\" data-end=\"206\">\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"62\" data-end=\"206\">The 'holidays' table contains the columns 'id', 'name', and 'date'. Each row represents a holiday occurring on a specific calendar date.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identify all holidays by considering weekends (i.e., Saturdays and Sundays) as holidays by default, even if they are not explicitly listed, along with the specific dates provided in the 'holiday' table.</li>\n<li>Identify all dates that would be considered a \"potential sandwich\". A potential sandwich date is defined as a workday that falls between two holidays.</li>\n<li>A date qualifies as a potential sandwich if both the previous and the next days are holidays, but the date itself is not.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include only the column 'potential_sandwich', listing all such dates in ascending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE holidays (\n  id INT,\n  name VARCHAR(255),\n  date DATE\n);\n\n-- Insert sample US holidays (assume year 2024)\nINSERT INTO holidays VALUES\n(1, 'Independence Day', '2024-07-04'),      -- Thursday\n(2, 'Labor Day', '2024-09-02'),             -- Monday\n(3, 'Thanksgiving Day', '2024-11-28'),      -- Thursday\n(4, 'Day after Thanksgiving', '2024-11-29'),-- Friday\n(5, 'Christmas Day', '2024-12-25'),         -- Wednesday\n(6, 'New Years Day', '2024-01-01'),       -- Monday\n(7, 'Memorial Day', '2024-05-27');          -- Monday",
        "slug": "mr-perfect",
        "originalCategory": "subqueries-ctes",
        "tags": ["Recursive CTEs","date handling"],
        "sample_testcases": [{"input":"CREATE TABLE holidays (\n  id INT,\n  name VARCHAR(255),\n  date DATE\n);\n\n-- Insert sample US holidays (assume year 2024)\nINSERT INTO holidays VALUES\n(1, 'Independence Day', '2024-07-04'),      -- Thursday\n(2, 'Labor Day', '2024-09-02'),             -- Monday\n(3, 'Thanksgiving Day', '2024-11-28'),      -- Thursday\n(4, 'Day after Thanksgiving', '2024-11-29'),-- Friday\n(5, 'Christmas Day', '2024-12-25'),         -- Wednesday\n(6, 'New Years Day', '2024-01-01'),       -- Monday\n(7, 'Memorial Day', '2024-05-27');          -- Monday","output":"potential_sandwich\n2024-07-05\n","explanation":"<p><strong>holidays:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>id</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>name</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>date</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Independence Day</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2024-07-04</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Labor Day</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2024-09-02</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Thanksgiving Day</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2024-11-28</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Day after Thanksgiving</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2024-11-29</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>5</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Christmas Day</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2024-12-25</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>6</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>New Years Day</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2024-01-01</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>7</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Memorial Day</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2024-05-27</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"},{"input":"CREATE TABLE holidays (\n  id INT,\n  name VARCHAR(255),\n  date DATE\n);\n\nINSERT INTO holidays VALUES\n(1, 'Independence Day', '2025-08-15'),\n(2, 'Janmashtami', '2025-08-16'),\n(3, 'Gandhi Jayanti', '2025-10-02'),\n(4, 'Diwali', '2025-10-21');","output":"potential_sandwich\n2025-10-03\n2025-10-20\n","explanation":"<p><strong>holidays:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>id</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>name</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>date</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>1</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Independence Day</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2025-08-15</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Janmashtami</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2025-08-16</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>3</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Gandhi Jayanti</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2025-10-02</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<p><strong>4</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>Diwali</strong></p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p><strong>2025-10-21</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"}]
