        "id": "569988",
        "title": "Thermal Thieves",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p>The climate control team at Olympus Base was sweating&mdash;and not just because of the thin Martian atmosphere. January 2025 had brought unexplained temperature spikes across research zones, threatening sensitive experiments. As the base's environmental analyst, you were tasked with identifying which sensors were reporting dangerous heat levels and pinpointing exactly when each one peaked.</p>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"378\" data-end=\"429\">You are given two tables: &lsquo;sensors&rsquo; and &lsquo;readings&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"433\" data-end=\"556\">The &lsquo;sensors&rsquo; table has &lsquo;sensor_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;location&rsquo;, and &lsquo;model&rsquo;. &lsquo;sensor_id&rsquo; is primary key; each row identifies one device.</li>\n<li data-start=\"559\" data-end=\"721\">The &lsquo;readings&rsquo; table has &lsquo;reading_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;sensor_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;timestamp&rsquo;, and &lsquo;temperature&rsquo;. &lsquo;reading_id&rsquo; is primary key; each row logs an hourly temperature for a sensor.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"723\" data-end=\"739\">Your task is to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"742\" data-end=\"811\">focus on readings from &lsquo;2025-01-01 00:00:00&rsquo; to &lsquo;2025-01-31 23:59:59&rsquo;</li>\n<li data-start=\"814\" data-end=\"894\">compute each sensor&rsquo;s average temperature and the overall average in that period</li>\n<li data-start=\"897\" data-end=\"1004\">select sensors whose average exceeds the overall average and report when each recorded its peak temperature</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"\" data-start=\"1006\" data-end=\"1153\">The output columns should be &lsquo;sensor_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;location&rsquo;, &lsquo;avg_temp&rsquo;, and &lsquo;peak_time&rsquo;, ordered by &lsquo;avg_temp&rsquo; descending, then by &lsquo;sensor_id&rsquo; ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE sensors (\n  sensor_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  location VARCHAR(100),\n  model VARCHAR(50)\n);\nCREATE TABLE readings (\n  reading_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  sensor_id INT,\n  timestamp TIMESTAMP,\n  temperature DECIMAL(5,2)\n);\nINSERT INTO sensors VALUES\n  (1, 'North Ridge', 'MX-1'),\n  (2, 'South Crater', 'MX-2'),\n  (3, 'East Plateau', 'MX-3');\nINSERT INTO readings VALUES\n  (1, 1, '2025-01-10 08:00:00', -65.50),\n  (2, 1, '2025-01-20 14:00:00', -60.00),\n  (3, 2, '2025-01-05 09:00:00', -55.25),\n  (4, 2, '2025-01-25 16:00:00', -50.00),\n  (5, 3, '2025-01-15 12:00:00', -70.00),\n  (6, 3, '2025-01-30 18:00:00', -65.00);",
        "slug": "thermal-thieves",
        "originalCategory": "subqueries-ctes",
        "tags": ["SubQueries","group by","Aggregation Functions"],
