        "title": "Stale Brews",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p>The Alchemancer&rsquo;s Guild sponsors virtual testing of its latest concoctions in the popular game &ldquo;Mystic Quests.&rdquo; To keep their catalogue fresh, they need to retire any brew that was created over 30 days ago and has not been tested in the past week.</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: &lsquo;potions&rsquo; and &lsquo;sessions&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The &lsquo;potions&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;potion_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;name&rsquo;, and &lsquo;brew_date&rsquo;. Each row logs when a brew was crafted.</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;sessions&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;session_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;potion_id&rsquo;, and &lsquo;test_date&rsquo;. Each row records a game session in which a potion was tested.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"403\" data-end=\"421\">You are tasked to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"425\" data-end=\"518\">Identify potions that were brewed more than 30 days before the reference date 2025-05-27.</li>\n<li data-start=\"521\" data-end=\"649\">From those, filter potions that either haven't been tested in over 7 days as of 2025-05-27&nbsp;or have never been tested at all.</li>\n<li data-start=\"652\" data-end=\"801\">For each selected potion, calculate the number of days since it was brewed and the number of days since it was last tested (or NULL if never tested).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The output columns should be &lsquo;potion_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;name&rsquo;, &lsquo;days_since_brew&rsquo;, and &lsquo;last_test_gap&rsquo;, ordered by &lsquo;days_since_brew&rsquo; descending, then by &lsquo;potion_id&rsquo; ascending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE potions (\n  potion_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  name VARCHAR(100),\n  brew_date DATE\n);\nCREATE TABLE sessions (\n  session_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n  potion_id INT,\n  test_date DATE\n);\nINSERT INTO potions VALUES\n  (1, 'Healing Draught',    '2025-03-15'),\n  (2, 'Mana Elixir',        '2025-03-20'),\n  (3, 'Invisibility Brew',  '2025-04-10'),\n  (4, 'Fire Resistance',    '2025-05-01'),\n  (5, 'Water Breathing',    '2025-03-01');\nINSERT INTO sessions VALUES\n  (1, 1, '2025-05-10'),\n  (2, 2, '2025-05-25'),\n  (3, 3, '2025-05-18'),\n  (4, 1, '2025-05-15'),\n  (5, 5, '2025-04-20');\n\n",
