        "title": "Blockbuster Actor Fee Analysis",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p>Film studios produce high-budget movies with substantial actor payments. Accountants require a report identifying blockbuster movies (budget &gt; $100M) from studios founded after 1950 where total actor fees exceeded $10M and constituted at least 10% of the movie's budget. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given three tables: 'studios', 'movies', and 'actors': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'studios' table includes the columns 'studio_id', 'studio_name', and 'founded_year', representing unique studio identifiers, studio names, and founding years. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'movies' table includes the columns 'movie_id', 'studio_id', 'title', and 'budget', representing unique movie identifiers, studio IDs, movie titles, and production budgets in dollars. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'actors' table includes the columns 'actor_id', 'movie_id', 'actor_name', and 'fee', representing unique actor identifiers, movie IDs, actor names, and fees paid in dollars. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that: &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Identifies movies from studios founded after 1950 with budgets exceeding $100,000,000. &nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li>For each selected movie, ensures there exists at least one actor group whose total fees exceed 10,000,000 and are at least 10% of the movie&rsquo;s budget.</li>\n<li>For qualifying movies, calculates total actor fees. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include columns 'studio_name', 'title', 'total_fees', and 'budget', ordered by studio_name ascending and total_fees descending.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE studios (\n    studio_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    studio_name VARCHAR(50),\n    founded_year INT\n);\nINSERT INTO studios VALUES\n(1, 'Old Hollywood Studio', 1930),\n(2, 'Modern Blockbusters Inc', 1960),\n(3, 'Millennium Films', 2000);\n\nCREATE TABLE movies (\n    movie_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    studio_id INT,\n    title VARCHAR(50),\n    budget DECIMAL(14,2)\n);\nINSERT INTO movies VALUES\n(101, 1, 'Classic Epic', 200000000.00),\n(102, 2, 'Galaxy Warriors', 150000000.00),\n(103, 2, 'Ocean Frontier', 120000000.00),\n(104, 3, 'Digital Dreams', 300000000.00);\n\nCREATE TABLE actors (\n    actor_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    movie_id INT,\n    actor_name VARCHAR(50),\n    fee DECIMAL(10,2)\n);\nINSERT INTO actors VALUES\n(1001, 102, 'Alex Nova', 8000000.00),\n(1002, 102, 'Taylor Rex', 12000000.00),\n(1003, 103, 'Jamie Wave', 6000000.00),\n(1004, 103, 'Riley Storm', 5000000.00),\n(1005, 104, 'Morgan Byte', 25000000.00);\n\n",
