        "id": "573672",
        "title": "Phantom Animal Hackers",
        "difficulty": "medium",
        "description": "<p>The cyberpunk city's holographic zoo reported a security breach coinciding with rare phantom animal feedings. Investigators need to identify hackers who breached critical systems during the same week as phantom/ghost species feedings to uncover potential bio-data theft. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: 'hackers' and 'animals': &nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The 'hackers' table includes the columns 'hacker_id', 'hacker_alias', 'system_breached', and 'breach_date', representing unique hacker identifiers, hacker aliases, breached system names, and breach timestamps. &nbsp;</li>\n<li>The 'animals' table includes the columns 'animal_id', 'species_name', 'exhibit_zone', and 'last_feeding_time', representing unique animal identifiers, species names, exhibit zones, and last feeding timestamps. &nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Your task is to write a SQL query that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Filters for hackers whose 'system_breached' is either 'Central Mainframe' or 'Zoo Security'.</li>\n<li>Checks for each such hacker whether there exists at least one animal with 'species_name' containing 'Phantom' or 'Ghost' whose 'last_feeding_time' falls in the same ISO week as the hacker&rsquo;s 'breach_date'.</li>\n<li>Selects distinct 'hacker_alias' values for hackers meeting both conditions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The final output should include the column 'hacker_alias', ordered by 'hacker_alias' in ascending order.</p>",
        "schema": "CREATE TABLE hackers (\n    hacker_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    hacker_alias VARCHAR(50),\n    system_breached VARCHAR(50),\n    breach_date DATETIME\n);\nINSERT INTO hackers VALUES\n(1, 'NeonSpectre', 'Zoo Security', '2023-11-20 14:30:00'),\n(2, 'VoidCrawler', 'Central Mainframe', '2023-11-19 22:15:00'),\n(3, 'DataPhantom', 'Bank Network', '2023-11-21 09:45:00'),\n(4, 'GhostByte', 'Zoo Security', '2023-11-23 16:20:00');\n\nCREATE TABLE animals (\n    animal_id INT PRIMARY KEY,\n    species_name VARCHAR(50),\n    exhibit_zone VARCHAR(50),\n    last_feeding_time DATETIME\n);\nINSERT INTO animals VALUES\n(101, 'Ghost Panther', 'Nocturnal Canyon', '2023-11-20 10:00:00'),\n(102, 'Phantom Owl', 'Sky Aviary', '2023-11-24 15:30:00'),\n(103, 'Silver Fox', 'Desert Dunes', '2023-11-18 11:00:00');\n\n",
